## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of AWS patching automation, SAP patching options, health checks, rollback strategies, and CloudFormation for operational guardrails.

## Key Concepts
- AWS Systems Manager Maintenance Windows
- SAP patching options: SUM vs OS patches
- Pre/post patch validation: SAPControl, SAP background jobs, host metrics
- Rollback strategies: SAP backups, AMI snapshots
- CloudFormation for roles and patch baselines

## Code Example
```javascript
// CFN skeleton (pseudo)
{
  "AWSTemplateFormatVersion": "2010-09-09",
  "Resources": {
    "SAPSSMRole": {
      "Type": "AWS::IAM::Role",
      "Properties": {
        "AssumeRolePolicyDocument": { "Version": "2012-10-17", "Statement": [ { "Effect": "Allow", "Principal": { "Service": ["ec2.amazonaws.com", "ssm.amazonaws.com"] }, "Action": "sts:AssumeRole" } ] },
        "ManagedPolicyArns": [ "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonSSMFullAccess" ]
      }
    },
    "SAPPatchBaseline": {
      "Type": "AWS::SSM::PatchBaseline",
      "Properties": {
        "Name": "SAPBaseline",
        "OperatingSystem": "AmazonLinux2"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify patch success in SAP and the OS without impacting production?
- How would you extend to multi-region DR alignment and scoped approvals?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical incident response design using AWS-native tooling in a SAP on AWS context, focusing on automation, speed, and auditable notifications.

## Key Concepts
- CloudWatch alarms and SAP heartbeat monitoring
- EventBridge as automation trigger
- Step Functions orchestration for multi-step recovery
- SSM Run Command for SAP status verification
- VPC security controls for subnet isolation
- SNS for stakeholder notifications

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Lambda skeleton for status check (conceptual)
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const ssm = new AWS.SSM();

exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const params = {
    InstanceIds: ['i-sap-instance'],
    DocumentName: 'AWS-RunShellScript',
    Parameters: {
      commands: ['HDB info | grep -i "overall status"']
    }
  };

  const result = await ssm.sendCommand(params).promise();
  return { status: 'checked', commandId: result.Command.CommandId };
};
```

